\\Lambda_{QCD}.description:
An intrinsic energy scale parameter of Quantum Chromodynamics, experimentally determined to be around 200-300 MeV (
\(\approx 3.2-4.8 \times 10^{-11} \text{J}\)
). It marks the energy threshold where the strong coupling becomes very large, indicating the onset of non-perturbative effects and quark confinement.
